# elevation_zscore
# The Z-score of Elevation, normalizing the elevation feature to account for variance across the dataset.
# Usefulness: Elevation is a key feature and has a wide range. Normalizing it helps downstream models focus on relative elevation differences without being affected by raw magnitude differences. Models may benefit as high-elevation areas have distinct vegetation and soil characteristics.
df['Elevation_Zscore'] = (df['Elevation'] - df['Elevation'].mean()) / df['Elevation'].std()

